{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"d0ab0e42f795c99e75971caba10d92e7c022da7e02aeeb1d37a9daf0ff1419fc","digest":{"component_or_area":"module-size enforcement and linting gates","key_entities":[".github/module-size-allowlist.txt",".github/module-size-ceilings.txt","tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py","gerrit-verify.yaml","test.yml","docs/architecture.md","src/rebar/**/*.py",".github/module-size-limit.txt"],"problem_keywords":["module-size limit","allowlist","grandfathering","escape hatch","refactoring","governance","hard gate","code quality"],"propositions":["Twelve src/rebar Python modules are currently grandfathered over the 800 LOC soft cap via allowlist and ceiling exemptions.","The allowlist/ceilings escape-hatch mechanism must be removed entirely so the 800 LOC limit becomes absolute and unenforced-against for no module.","Each of the 12 grandfathered modules must be split along a logical call-graph seam (producing no <100-LOC files) and landed independently on main via Gerrit.","After all splits complete, the allowlist and ceilings files, the sync contract test, and the shell gate's allowlist branch must be deleted.","A hard gate must be added to prevent the module-size limit itself from being changed through the normal contribution process, requiring admin manual override."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787316571787972001,"uuid":"af6c3eb8-f085-4669-83ef-5b4e31c8fd4d"}